        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Self-crafting needs two Engineering skill tracks and a specialization; buying the finished toy bypasses that work.\n\n1. For collection alone, buy an unused Gnomish Gravity Well (40727) from the Auction House or another Engineer, then use it to add it to the Toy Box. If you want to craft or operate it yourself, continue with the profession route below.\n\n2. Visit Lilliam Sparkspindle at 62.8,32.0 in Stormwind or Roxxik at 56.8,56.4 in Orgrimmar. Learn Engineering and its separate Cataclysm branch. Raise Cataclysm Engineering to 50 using the trainer's available recipes; levels in another expansion's Engineering do not count.\n\n3. If you are not a Gnomish Engineer, raise Classic Engineering to 200 and take Gnomish Engineering from a capital Engineering trainer. Turn in 6 Mithril Tubes, 1 Accurate Scope and 2 Advanced Target Dummies. Any eligible race can choose this specialization. Return to the trainer and learn Gnomish Gravity Well.\n\n4. Gather 6 Electrified Ether and 3 Hardened Elementium Bars. Ether is crafted from Volatile Air; the bars require Elementium Bars and Volatile Earth. Buying the finished reagents is sufficient. Bring an Arclight Spanner and Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor, or a tool replacing them, and craft the toy.\n\n5. Use the finished item to learn it. To activate it from the Toy Box, keep Cataclysm Engineering 50 and Gnomish Engineering. Use it out of combat in a supported flying area; each activation raises you again, but overheating can leave you falling.",
