        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Buying the toy is simple, but using it requires Cataclysm Engineering 70 and the associated material investment.\n\n1. Buy an unused Loot-A-Rang (60854), commission it from an Engineer, or craft it yourself. Check the item ID: Findle's Loot-A-Rang is a separate toy with different location restrictions.\n\n2. For self-crafting or use, visit Lilliam Sparkspindle at 62.8,32.0 in Stormwind or Roxxik at 56.8,56.4 in Orgrimmar. Train Engineering and Cataclysm Engineering. Reach Cataclysm skill 40 and learn Loot-a-Rang from the trainer.\n\n3. Obtain 5 Hardened Elementium Bars and 5 Electrified Ether. Making the bars takes 50 Elementium Bars and 20 Volatile Earth. Ether is made from Volatile Air in batches of 2-3; buy 5 finished Ether or craft enough batches. At an anvil, craft Loot-A-Rang.\n\n4. Use the item to add it to the Toy Box. To operate it, continue leveling Cataclysm Engineering to 70 even though the toy was craftable at 40. Early recipes include Handful of Obsidium Bolts, Electrified Ether and Explosive Bolts; later use trainer recipes such as the fishing tools and Volatile Seaforium Blastpack while they still grant skill.\n\n5. Put the learned toy on your action bar. With Cataclysm Engineering 70, activate it near lootable corpses to retrieve their loot. Auto Loot makes repeated use easier; a corpse must still be in range and eligible for your loot.",
