        itemId = 63269,
        name = "Loaded Gnomish Dice",
        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - The direct route is Rogue-only and can require thousands of pickpockets with no guaranteed drop.\n\n1. If you are not a Rogue or want to avoid the farm, buy unused Loaded Gnomish Dice (63269) from another player and go to step 7. For farming, bring a Rogue with Stealth and Pick Pocket, enable Auto Loot and leave bag space for lockboxes and junk.\n\n2. Travel to Maker's Ascent in northwest Uldum. Begin at the bottom of the stairs around 42.0,12.5 and work upward toward the Ruins of Khintaset. Use the original Uldum phase: if assaults have replaced the zone, speak to Zidormi near 56.0,35.1 to return to the earlier version.\n\n3. Pick Pocket the Schnottz Infantrymen in each formation. Aim Distract into the center of a patrol to hold it briefly while you work; later replies also confirm that Sapping its elite leader stops the formation. Pick each normal soldier and the elite separately, watching for movement as the control expires.\n\n4. Pick the stationary Infantrymen at the edges of each platform too. Continue up the steps without skipping a formation. Avoid campfires and careless movement through enemies, which can break Stealth. The dice must come from Pick Pocket; killing alone is not this route.\n\n5. At the gate above the stairs, open lockboxes you can unlock, sell junk and free bag space. Return to the bottom for another circuit when pockets have refilled. If you kill picked enemies for fresh respawns, coordinate with any other Rogue already using the route.\n\n6. Repeat until the dice appear in your bags. If this phase of Maker's Ascent has no Infantrymen or is crowded, try the humanoids in the Chamber of the Moon below the Obelisk of the Moon, entering near 42.0,25.0. Alternatively, use Tol Barad Peninsula's Rustberg Village around 67.0,28.0 and Farson Hold around 37.4,29.4 as pocket circuits. These are alternatives, not additional required steps.\n\n7. Use the unused dice from your bags to learn the account-wide toy. A learned copy cannot be sold, so keep any extra unused copies separate if you intend to trade them.",
