        name = "Blessing of the Old God",
        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Nerubian sites are sparse and repeated random project rolls can make the direct route lengthy.\n\n1. Learn Archaeology from Harrison Jones at 85.6,25.8 in Stormwind, or Belloc Brightblade at 49.0,70.6 in Orgrimmar. Enable dig-site tracking on the world map and learn Survey. This is a secondary profession and does not replace a primary profession.\n\n2. Raise Archaeology to 375 to open Northrend dig sites. Fly between the active Nerubian sites shown on your map. These are sparse, so finish unwanted Vrykul and other active sites to roll new locations; Vrykul fragments do not become Nerubian fragments by themselves.\n\n3. At each active dig site, use Survey, follow the instrument's direction and narrow the distance as its light changes from red through yellow to green. Loot the finds until the site is exhausted. In the Archaeology journal, solve the current Nerubian artifact to roll the next project. Continue until Blessing of the Old God appears; neither a specific dig nor a fixed solve count guarantees this rare.\n\n4. Optional fragment supply at Archaeology 600: crate completed common artifacts from Pandaria, Draenor or the Broken Isles into Restored Artifacts. Visit Brann Bronzebeard at 83.5,31.0 in the Seat of Knowledge, on the balcony above Mogu'shan Palace in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms. Exchange 1 Restored Artifact for a crate of Nerubian fragments and open it. Ordinary old Nerubian solves are not themselves Restored Artifacts.\n\n5. For a concentrated optional Restored Artifact farm, first reach Exalted with the Lorewalkers. Buy Brann's Mantid Artifact Hunter's Kit for 2 Restored Artifacts, open it, keep the Sonic Locator in your bags and use its Lorewalker's Map. Survey the resulting Mantid sites in Townlong Steppes and Dread Wastes, solve and crate the common artifacts, then return to Brann for Nerubian crates. The locator lasts one real-time day; this route supplies fragments but does not guarantee the next rare project.\n\n6. When Blessing of the Old God is your current Nerubian project, collect 140 Nerubian Archaeology Fragments, or insert up to 3 Nerubian Obelisks into its sockets. Each socket replaces 12 fragments; all three reduce the requirement to 104 fragments. Click Solve to receive the toy.\n\n7. Use the completed Blessing of the Old God from your bags to add it to the account-wide Toy Box. The finished toy does not require Archaeology to use. Despite the Qiraji appearance, this comes from Nerubian Archaeology in Northrend. It is not a Tol'vir or Ahn'Qiraj drop.",
