                step = 4,
                label = "Brann - OPTIONAL fragment exchange, upper balcony",
                mapName = "Vale of Eternal Blossoms",
            },
        },
        areaMaps = { 12 },
        itemId = 64651,
        name = "Wisp Amulet",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - The rare project may take many Night Elf solves, with no fixed discovery order.\n\n1. Learn Archaeology from Harrison Jones at 85.6,25.8 in Stormwind, or Belloc Brightblade at 49.0,70.6 in Orgrimmar. Enable dig-site tracking on the world map and learn Survey. This is a secondary profession and does not replace a primary profession.\n\n2. Use Kalimdor's active Night Elf dig sites. Night Elf ruins are common there; check the race shown on each find. Completing Fossil or other active sites can make room for new Night Elf sites.\n\n3. At each active dig site, use Survey, follow the instrument's direction and narrow the distance as its light changes from red through yellow to green. Loot the finds until the site is exhausted. In the Archaeology journal, solve the current Night Elf artifact to roll the next project. Continue until Wisp Amulet appears; neither a specific dig nor a fixed solve count guarantees this rare.\n\n4. Optional fragment supply at Archaeology 600: crate completed common artifacts from Pandaria, Draenor or the Broken Isles into Restored Artifacts. Visit Brann Bronzebeard at 83.5,31.0 in the Seat of Knowledge, on the balcony above Mogu'shan Palace in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms. Exchange 1 Restored Artifact for a crate of Night Elf fragments and open it. Ordinary old Night Elf solves are not themselves Restored Artifacts.\n\n5. When Wisp Amulet is your current Night Elf project, collect 150 Night Elf Archaeology Fragments, or insert up to 3 Highborne Scrolls into its sockets. Each socket replaces 12 fragments; all three reduce the requirement to 114 fragments. Click Solve to receive the toy.\n\n6. Use the completed Wisp Amulet from your bags to add it to the account-wide Toy Box. The finished toy does not require Archaeology to use. Any race can use the learned toy. It is a cosmetic form, not a flying mount or the Night Elf death-release racial.",
        sourceType = "Professions",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=64651",
    },
