        name = "Pendant of the Scarab Storm",
        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Tol'vir sites share Kalimdor's limited active-site slots, and the rare project is random.\n\n1. Learn Archaeology from Harrison Jones at 85.6,25.8 in Stormwind, or Belloc Brightblade at 49.0,70.6 in Orgrimmar. Enable dig-site tracking on the world map and learn Survey. This is a secondary profession and does not replace a primary profession.\n\n2. Raise Archaeology to 450 to open Uldum's Tol'vir sites. Survey active Uldum sites and clear other Kalimdor sites when needed to generate replacements. If an assault phase hides the original sites, speak to Zidormi at 56.0,35.1 to return to earlier Uldum.\n\n3. At each active dig site, use Survey, follow the instrument's direction and narrow the distance as its light changes from red through yellow to green. Loot the finds until the site is exhausted. In the Archaeology journal, solve the current Tol'vir artifact to roll the next project. Continue until Pendant of the Scarab Storm appears; neither a specific dig nor a fixed solve count guarantees this rare.\n\n4. Optional fragment supply at Archaeology 600: crate completed common artifacts from Pandaria, Draenor or the Broken Isles into Restored Artifacts. Visit Brann Bronzebeard at 83.5,31.0 in the Seat of Knowledge, on the balcony above Mogu'shan Palace in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms. Exchange 1 Restored Artifact for a crate of Tol'vir fragments and open it. Ordinary old Tol'vir solves are not themselves Restored Artifacts.\n\n5. For a concentrated optional Restored Artifact farm, first reach Exalted with the Lorewalkers. Buy Brann's Mantid Artifact Hunter's Kit for 2 Restored Artifacts, open it, keep the Sonic Locator in your bags and use its Lorewalker's Map. Survey the resulting Mantid sites in Townlong Steppes and Dread Wastes, solve and crate the common artifacts, then return to Brann for Tol'vir crates. The locator lasts one real-time day; this route supplies fragments but does not guarantee the next rare project.\n\n6. When Pendant of the Scarab Storm is your current Tol'vir project, collect 150 Tol'vir Archaeology Fragments, or insert up to 3 Tol'vir Hieroglyphics into its sockets. Each socket replaces 12 fragments; all three reduce the requirement to 114 fragments. Click Solve to receive the toy.\n\n7. Use the completed Pendant of the Scarab Storm from your bags to add it to the account-wide Toy Box. The finished toy does not require Archaeology to use. The scarabs are cosmetic rather than a combat swarm. If Uldum sites are scarce, the optional Restored Artifact route avoids repeatedly flying across Kalimdor for new site rolls.",
